    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0180" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v20/pg152"/>

                <head>75. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Israel<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d75-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1968-02-09T00:48:00+00:00">February 9, 1968,
                        0048Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>112564. Subject: Tiran Island. Following based on uncleared memcon. Noforn,FYI
                    and subject revision.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>In course farewell call by Israeli Ambassador Harman, Secretary said he
                        was disappointed by GOI reply (State 111432)<anchor n="2" xml:id="d75-f2"/>
                        to his January 17 letter to Eban on Tiran Island.<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d75-f3"/> Secretary said he viewed response as thinly-disguised
                        “no.” Added he thought it unreasonable to expect SAG promise island would
                        remain permanently uninhabited. Evacuation island was tiny gesture Israel
                        could easily make.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item> Harman replied potential danger of island must not be overlooked. Guns
                        located there could close Strait Tiran. Secretary replied <pb facs="0181"
                            n="153" xml:id="pg153"/> militarization was not issue; GOI was seeking
                        SAG assurance island would never be inhabited.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item> Harman asked whether SAG agreeable leave Tiran demilitarized. Secretary
                        said this point covered in his letter to Eban. Harman said he would convey
                        Secretary’s concern to Foreign Minister.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
